# For docker-compose.prod.yml, on the VM. Copy it to .env there (it is ignored by git). It has only
# what is NOT secret: the passwords are in the OCI Vault (secrets aireuskadi-postgres-password,
# aireuskadi-reader-password, aireuskadi-auth-password and aireuskadi-jwt-secret).
# deploy/fetch-secrets.sh reads them with the identity of the VM and writes
# them in /run/aireuskadi/secrets.env (memory), and deploy/aireuskadi.service gives both files to docker
# compose. Nobody types or copies a password.
POSTGRES_DB=aireuskadi
POSTGRES_USER=aireuskadi
# The read-only role of the services that only read.
POSTGRES_READER_USER=aireuskadi_reader
# The role of the auth service, which reads the accounts.
POSTGRES_AUTH_USER=aireuskadi_auth
# The account of the site that is the full admin of Grafana. Grafana reads it only the first time
# it starts (its volume grafana-data keeps it): choose it before the first `up`.
GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=
# Only for a try WITHOUT the Vault (never on the VM): the passwords here, of letters, digits, "-"
# and "_" only (they go inside a URL; a "/", "+", "@" or ":" breaks it) and not the ones of the
# laptop. JWT_SECRET: at least 32 characters.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_READER_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_AUTH_PASSWORD=
# JWT_SECRET=

# Where the images are, and which one. :pro is what deploy-pro.yml publishes.
GHCR_OWNER=asieramigorena
IMAGE_TAG=pro


# The tunnel is optional. To turn it on, uncomment this line.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=tunnel
# The Tailscale auth key of the tunnel (Settings -> Keys, not reusable, tag:aireuskadi) is a secret too:
# it is the secret aireuskadi-tailscale-authkey of the Vault, and fetch-secrets.sh puts it in
# TS_AUTHKEY. It is only read the first time: afterwards the identity is in the tailscale-state
# volume. Without that secret the stack starts without the tunnel key.
# For a try WITHOUT the Vault (never on the VM): TS_AUTHKEY=...

# The tunnel of Cloudflare, for a domain of our own (use one tunnel, not both): to turn it on, put
# cloudflare in COMPOSE_PROFILES instead of tunnel. Its token is the secret
# aireuskadi-cloudflare-token of the Vault, and fetch-secrets.sh puts it in CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN.
# Turn it on only once that secret exists: without it cloudflared starts again and again.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=cloudflare
